2. Preserve the canonical entry conditions

The baseline entry logic must continue to:

1. Use completed five-minute candles.
2. Mark the opening high and low from the first completed five-minute candle.
3. Require the option premium to break below the opening low.
4. Identify a subsequent recovery or reversal structure using only information available at that time.
5. Identify the eligible causal swing high.
6. Enter at the completed candle close when the premium breaks the eligible swing high before reaching the opening high.
7. Permit the entry candle to close below the opening high, as allowed by the existing rule.
8. Match the exact option contract and expiry.

Do not use future candles to determine entries, swing highs, stop adjustments or target decisions.

Do not alter the canonical entry conditions merely to improve backtest results. Investigate entry improvements separately if a concrete defect is identified.

