4. Mandatory overall target and stop-loss report

This is a primary deliverable, not an optional appendix.

For every candidate, produce the following counts across all eligible, usable historical entries, including all eligible periods that can be reconstructed reliably.

Required metric	What to count
Total detected setups	All setups found by the canonical entry detector
Eligible entries	Setups that satisfy the canonical entry rules
Simulated entries	Entries with a valid entry price and usable simulation
Target exits	Trades that actually exited at the target while the position was open
Stop-loss exits	Trades that actually exited at the stop while the position was open
Ambiguous exits	Trades where the stop and target were both touched and order cannot be determined
End-of-session exits	Trades closed under an explicitly identified experimental session-close rule
Other exits	Any other separately defined exit category
Unresolved entries	Trades without sufficient subsequent candle data to classify the outcome
Skipped entries	Entries not taken, with exact reasons
Invalid entries	Entries with invalid risk, price or contract data

For every metric, report both the count and, where meaningful, its percentage of the appropriate denominator.

Do not calculate target-hit or stop-loss percentages using all detected setups if only a subset was eligible or simulated. Clearly label every denominator.

