Count reconciliation

For each candidate, verify that the simulated entries reconcile with mutually exclusive outcomes:

Simulated entries = target exits + stop-loss exits + ambiguous exits + end-of-session exits + other exits + unresolved entries

Adapt this identity only when the simulator’s documented definitions require it, and explain every exception.

Ensure a trade is counted only once in its final exit category. A later target touch after the position has already stopped out must not count as a target exit.

If the existing data does not support exact overall counts, report the exact count for the reconstructable subset and the number of entries whose outcomes cannot be established. Never estimate missing outcomes.

